  "chapter": {
    "number": 19,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(20) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord hear you in the day of trouble; the name of the God of Jacob defend you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Send you help from the sanctuary, and aid you out of Sion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Remember all your",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 38
          },
          {
            "text": "sacrifice, and enrich your whole burnt offering. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Grant you according to your heart, and fulfill all your desire.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "We will exult in your salvation, and in the name of our God shall we be magnified: the Lord fulfil all your petitions.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Now I know that the Lord has saved his Christ: he shall hear him from his holy heaven: the salvation of his right hand is mighty.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Some glory in chariots, and some in horses: but we will",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 39
          },
          {
            "text": "glory in the name of the Lord our God.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They are overthrown and fallen: but we are risen, and have been set upright.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, save the king: and hear us in whatever day we call upon you.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 38,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, meat offering.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 19,
          "verse": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 39,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. be magnified.",
        "reference": {
